
  iMac Display live system  (Arch Linux + Claude Code)
  Runs from the USB stick. The iMac's internal drive is not touched.

  1. Get internet. Pick one:
       Wi-Fi     iwctl station wlan0 connect "NETWORK NAME"
                 (other interface name? see: iwctl station list)
       iPhone    connect by USB, turn on Personal Hotspot, tap Trust
       Ethernet  plug in a cable from the router

  2. From the MacBook (easier for copy and paste):
       ssh root@imac-live.local
     or keep working on this console.

  3. Start Claude:
       cd /persist/imac-display && claude
     Log in with the link it shows, then tell it:
       follow docs/IMAC-BUILD.md

  Hardware facts in one file:  m0-check

